@format 1
@id functionality.media-loading
@title Load a media file
@section Functionality
@area Media discovery and import
@entry source-browse, source-enter, files-add, folder-add, viewer-drop, window-drop, merge-group-drop, worklist-relay, delivered-output, files-remove, files-clear, unload-current, unload-all, console-clear-tabs, relay-source-remove, batch-evict, funnel-drain, files-row-release, files-select-all, files-row-press, merge-group-row, startup-restore, relay-source
@summary Trace every current source path that can request a media load through discovery, probing, preview opening, state publication, and its terminal outcomes.
@tag media
@tag loading
@tag ffprobe
@tag preview
@tag source

@alias source = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PSource
@alias list = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PList
@alias docket = Cadroue.Application.LDocket
@alias group = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PGroup
@alias viewer = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PViewer
@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias workspace = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PWorkspace
@alias roster = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PRoster
@alias strip = Cadroue.UIShell.PControlBar.PStrip
@alias console = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PConsole
@alias app = Cadroue.UIShell.PProgram
@alias split = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PSplitTab
@alias edit = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PEditTab
@alias convert = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PConvertTab
@alias audio = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PAudioTab
@alias merge = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PMergeTab
@alias funnel = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.PFunnelTab
@alias librarian = Cadroue.Application.LLibrarian
@alias preference = Cadroue.Application.LPreference
@alias media-load = Cadroue.Media.LMediaLoad
@alias media = Cadroue.Media.LMedia
@alias custody = Cadroue.Core.LCustody
@alias info = Cadroue.UIShell.PPanels.PInfo

[source-browse] Source browse button <input>
- Open the source picker when the Browse button is clicked @ source.PSourceOpenHandle(...)
> source-entry-join

[source-enter] Source path Return key <input>
- Submit the typed source path when Return is pressed @ source.PSourceKeyHandle(...)
> source-entry-join

[files-add] Add files button <input>
- Invoke the registered Add Files callback from the list-button click @ list.PListButtonBuild(...)
- Open the multi-file media picker @ list.PListFilesOpen(...)
> files-picker-result

[folder-add] Add folder button <input>
- Invoke the registered Add Folder callback from the list-button click @ list.PListButtonBuild(...)
- Open the multi-folder picker @ list.PListFolderOpen(...)
> folder-picker-result

[viewer-drop] Viewer file drop <input>
- Receive a file-system drop on the viewer overlay @ viewer.PDropHandle(...)
> viewer-drop-route

[window-drop] Window file drop <input>
- Receive a file-system drop through the main-window routed drop handler @ window.PDropHandle(...)
> window-drop-route

[merge-group-drop] Merge group external file drop <input>
- Receive an external file drop on the Merge group area or an existing group card @ group.PGroupDropHandle(...)
  @ group.PGroupCardHandle(...)
- Resolve the dropped file-system paths through the Merge group's file-request delegate @ group.PGroupPathsRead(...)
- Submit those external paths to the Merge Files list before inserting them into the group @ list.PListPathsAdd(...)
> merge-scan-ready

[worklist-relay] Worklist relay to tab <input>
- Resolve and select the requested relay target before replacing its unlocked paths @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
> worklist-target-check

[delivered-output] Delivered processing output <input>
- Resolve the target or original tab that should receive the delivered path @ list.PListDeliveredAdd(...)
  @ list.PListDeliveredPlace(...)
> delivered-target-check

[files-remove] Remove selected files button <input>
- Invoke the registered Remove File callback from the list-button click @ list.PListButtonBuild(...)
- Resolve the selected unlocked paths, remember the first removed index, and request their removal @ list.PListRemove(...)
> removal-trigger-join

[files-clear] Remove all files button <input>
- Invoke the registered Remove All callback from the list-button click @ list.PListButtonBuild(...)
- Request removal of every currently unlocked Files entry @ list.PListClear(...)
> removal-trigger-join

[unload-current] Selected-workspace Unload command <input>
- Dispatch the configured Unload command to the selected workspace @ window.PShortcutMediaClose(...)
- Close the viewer and clear the workspace's unlocked Files entries @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaClear(...)
> removal-trigger-join

[unload-all] Unload All command <input>
- Dispatch the configured Unload All command to the tab strip @ window.PShortcutRun(...)
- Clear media content in every tab workspace @ strip.PStripContentClear(...)
- Each list-backed workspace requests removal of its unlocked Files entries @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaClear(...)
> removal-trigger-join

[console-clear-tabs] Worklist Clear Tabs command <input>
- After destructive confirmation, request media-content clearing for every tab @ console.PConsoleTabsHandle(...)
- Clear media content in every tab workspace @ strip.PStripContentClear(...)
> removal-trigger-join

[relay-source-remove] Post-delivery source removal <input>
- When relay-empty policy permits, request removal of delivered source and merge-source paths from their source tab @ list.PListDeliveredRemove(...)
> removal-trigger-join

[batch-evict] Worklist batch eviction <input>
- Request removal of listed media whose batch has left the worklist @ list.PListBatchEvict(...)
> removal-trigger-join

[funnel-drain] Funnel source drain <input>
- Run the configured Funnel drain callback and request removal of its paths from the selected tab's docket @ app.OnStartup(...)
> removal-trigger-join

[files-row-release] Files row mouse release <input>
- Receive MouseLeftButtonUp on a Files row and release the captured row interaction @ list.PListRowBuild(...)
> row-release-check

[files-select-all] Files Ctrl+A <input>
- Receive the Files panel key event and test whether Control+A can apply to the current selection @ list.PListKeyHandle(...)
> select-all-check

[files-row-press] Files row mouse press <input>
- Receive MouseLeftButtonDown on a Files row and pass the row to selection logic @ list.PListRowBuild(...)
- Apply normal, Control, or Shift selection for the pressed row @ list.PListPressHandle(...)
> selection-manual-ready

[merge-group-row] Merge group item selection <input>
- Emit the selected grouped media path when a Merge group row is pressed @ group.PGroupFileBuild(...)
> merge-group-open

[startup-restore] Automatic startup restore <input>
- Read the saved automatic-media preference and schedule the existing saved path for the active viewer @ window.PWindowMediaRestore(...)
> startup-check

[relay-source] Relay source arrival <input>
- Create and select the relay tab when a startup or live relay is accepted @ window.PWindowRelayAccept(...)
- Apply the relay payload to its workspace @ workspace.PWorkspaceRelayApply(...)
> relay-source-check

[source-entry-join] Source entry requests converge <junction>
> source-entry-check

[files-picker-result] Add-files picker result <decision>
- Submit the selected file paths to PListPathsAdd only when the picker was accepted @ list.PListFilesOpen(...)
? "Picker accepted" > scan-request-join
? "Picker cancelled" > no-load-input-join [left]

[folder-picker-result] Add-folder picker result <decision>
- Submit the selected folder paths to PListPathsAdd only when the picker was accepted @ list.PListFolderOpen(...)
? "Picker accepted" > scan-request-join
? "Picker cancelled" > no-load-input-join [left]

[viewer-drop-route] Viewer drop routing <decision>
- In list-backed mode, require at least one folder or supported media path; in direct-viewer mode, require an existing file not rejected by the audio-only policy @ viewer.PDropEffectRead(...)
- Forward all dropped paths through PDropPathsChange when a list-backed tab subscribed to the viewer drop @ viewer.PDropHandle(...)
- Otherwise choose the first dropped file and request it directly from the viewer @ viewer.PDropHandle(...)
? "List-backed drop accepted" > scan-request-join
? "Direct viewer file accepted" > viewer-request-join [right]
? "Drop rejected" > no-load-input-join [left]

[window-drop-route] Window drop routing <decision>
- Ignore drops owned by a Merge group; in list-backed mode require at least one folder or supported media path, while viewer-only mode accepts the first existing file unless blocked by the audio-only policy @ window.PDropHandle(...)
  @ window.PDropEffectRead(...)
- Forward all accepted paths to the active Files list when one exists @ window.PDropHandle(...)
- Otherwise choose the first accepted file for the active viewer @ window.PDropHandle(...)
? "Active list accepts drop" > scan-request-join
? "Viewer-only surface accepts file" > viewer-request-join [right]
? "Drop rejected or no viewer" > no-load-input-join [left]

[merge-scan-ready] Merge drop paths ready <junction>
> scan-request-join

[worklist-target-check] Worklist target availability <decision>
- Require the relay target surface to expose a Files docket, select that target, clear its unlocked paths, then submit the relayed paths for media scanning @ roster.PRosterRelaySend(...)
! Clearing an existing current path can synchronously publish a remaining locked path before the relay additions; a later newly added path may supersede that temporary viewer request.
? "Target docket available" > scan-request-join
? "Target docket unavailable" > no-load-input-join [left]

[delivered-target-check] Delivery target availability <decision>
- Require the requested destination tab to still expose a Files docket before scanning and adding the delivered path @ list.PListDeliveredAdd(...)
  @ list.PListDeliveredPlace(...)
? "Target docket available" > scan-request-join
? "Target docket unavailable" > no-load-input-join [left]

[removal-trigger-join] Removal requests converge <junction>
> docket-removal

[row-release-check] Row-release selection collapse <decision>
- Collapse a previously retained multi-selection press to that row; otherwise leave the current path unchanged @ list.PListReleaseHandle(...)
? "Collapse path retained" > selection-manual-join
? "No collapse pending" > no-load-input-join [left]

[select-all-check] Select-all eligibility <decision>
- Require Control+A, an existing selection, and at least one docket path before applying the full selection @ list.PListKeyHandle(...)
- Republish the current path while applying the full selection @ list.PListSelectionApply(...)
? "Select all applied" > selection-manual-join
? "Key or selection guard rejected" > no-load-input-join [left]

[selection-manual-ready] Direct row selection routed to shared selection path <junction>
> selection-manual-join

[merge-group-open] Merge grouped-path adapter <process>
- Forward the selected grouped path to the Merge viewer through the same Merge selected-path method @ merge.PMergePathShow(...)
> viewer-request-join [right]

[startup-check] Saved source availability <decision>
- Require automatic media restore to be enabled, a nonblank saved path, and an existing file @ window.PWindowMediaRestore(...)
? "Saved source available" > viewer-request-join [right]
? "Restore condition not met" > no-load-input-join [left]

[relay-source-check] Relay source eligibility <decision>
- Require the relay workspace to have a viewer and the relay payload to contain a nonblank source path @ workspace.PWorkspaceRelayApply(...)
? "Viewer and source available" > viewer-request-join [right]
? "Viewer or source unavailable" > no-load-input-join [left]

[source-entry-check] Source entry acceptance <decision>
- Require an accepted picker result or an existing typed path, and reject audio-only media outside an Audio source bar @ source.PSourceOpenHandle(...)
  @ source.PSourceKeyHandle(...)
? "Accepted source" > viewer-request-join [right]
? "Cancelled, missing, or disallowed audio" > no-load-input-join [left]

[scan-request-join] Media scan requests converge <junction>
> list-scan

[docket-removal] Docket path removal <decision>
- Remove matching docket entries and publish LDocketRemoved only when at least one existing path is removed @ docket.LDocketPathsRemove(...)
? "At least one path removed" > removed-current-check
? "No matching path removed" > no-load-list-join [left]

[selection-manual-join] Manual selection paths converge <junction>
> selection-removal-ready

[no-load-input-join] Input-stage no-load outcomes converge <junction>
> no-load-input

[list-scan] Media path discovery <process>
- Keep supported existing media files supplied directly @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
- Recursively enumerate supplied folders, keep supported media, and order discovered files case-insensitively @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
- Skip inaccessible folders after recording I/O or access failures @ list.PListMediaScan(...)
> docket-add

[removed-current-check] Replacement selection after removal <decision>
- When the current path disappeared, the LDocketRemoved subscriber selects the first remaining docket path @ list.PListDocketRemoveHandle(...)
- After a direct Remove File operation returns from that notification, select the remaining path at the removed item's clamped prior index @ list.PListRemove(...)
! A direct Remove File can therefore publish one replacement during LDocketRemoved and immediately publish the clamped replacement afterward; the later viewer request can supersede the first.
? "Replacement path published" > selection-after-removal-join
? "No replacement path published" > no-load-list-join [left]

[selection-removal-ready] Manual selection shared line continues <junction>
> selection-after-removal-join

[no-load-input] Load not started — input stage <output>
= The initiating input path ends before a backend media request is started.

[docket-add] Docket insertion <decision>
- Create a batch when required, ignore paths already present, and add each new media entry to the docket @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
? "At least one new entry" > docket-added
? "Nothing new added" > no-load-list-join [left]

[selection-after-removal-join] Removal and manual selection paths converge <junction>
> selection-docket-ready

[docket-added] First new item activation <process>
- Publish the docket change and added-entry notification after insertion @ docket.LDocketPathsAdd(...)
- Select the first newly added entry when the Files panel receives the added-entry notification @ list.PListDocketAddHandle(...)
> selection-final-join

[selection-docket-ready] Shared selection line continues to docket-added stage <junction>
> selection-final-join

[selection-final-join] All Files selection publications converge <junction>
> list-selection

[list-selection] Current Files path publication <process>
- Set the current path, refresh visible selection, and publish PListPathChange @ list.PListCurrentApply(...)
> selected-path-check

[selected-path-check] Selected path availability <decision>
- Let each tab selected-path adapter ignore a null or blank current path before requesting its viewer @ split.PSplitPathShow(...)
  @ edit.PEditPathShow(...)
  @ convert.PConvertPathShow(...)
  @ audio.PAudioPathShow(...)
  @ merge.PMergePathShow(...)
  @ funnel.PFunnelPathShow(...)
? "Nonblank current path" > tab-path-adapter
? "No current path" > no-load-list-join [left]

[tab-path-adapter] Tab selected-path adapter <process>
- Request the selected nonblank path in a Split viewer @ split.PSplitPathShow(...)
- Request the selected nonblank path in an Edit viewer @ edit.PEditPathShow(...)
- Request the selected nonblank path in a Convert viewer @ convert.PConvertPathShow(...)
- Save and restore the Audio plan around the selected-path viewer request @ audio.PAudioPathShow(...)
- Request the selected nonblank path in a Merge viewer @ merge.PMergePathShow(...)
- Request the selected nonblank path in a Funnel viewer @ funnel.PFunnelPathShow(...)
> viewer-request-join [right]

[no-load-list-join] List-stage no-load outcomes converge <junction>
> no-load-list

[viewer-request-join] Viewer source requests converge <junction>
> viewer-request

[no-load-list] Load not started — list stage <output>
= List or docket handling ends without starting a backend media request.

[viewer-request] Viewer source gate <decision>
- Reject requests while viewer commands are inactive or the requested source is blank @ viewer.PViewerSourceOpen(...)
- Detect whether the requested source is a Cadroue sidecar file @ librarian.LLibrarianFileCheck(...)
? "Blank or inactive request" > no-load-viewer-join [left]
? "Sidecar source" > sidecar-resolve
? "Direct media source" > direct-media-ready

[sidecar-resolve] Sidecar source resolution <decision>
- Resolve the sidecar's recorded source through the Librarian seam @ viewer.PViewerSidecarResolve(...)
- Accept a verified source immediately, optionally accept a discovered mismatch, or ask the user to locate the media file @ viewer.PViewerSidecarResolve(...)
- Verify or explicitly accept a manually located mismatch before returning it @ viewer.PViewerSidecarFind(...)
? "Media source resolved" > source-remember-join
? "Read failed or source declined" > no-load-viewer-join [left]

[direct-media-ready] Direct media source ready <junction>
> source-remember-join

[no-load-viewer-join] Viewer-stage no-load outcomes converge <junction>
> no-load-viewer

[source-remember-join] Resolved media sources converge <junction>
> source-remember

[no-load-viewer] Load not started — viewer gate <output>
= The viewer rejects or cannot resolve the source before backend loading starts.

[source-remember] Last-media preference <storage>
- Store the resolved media path as the last-media preference @ preference.LPreferenceMediaSet(...)
> transform-reset

[transform-reset] Incoming-source transform reset <process>
- Reset rotation and flip to their defaults for the incoming source @ viewer.PViewerSourceOpen(...)
> engine-select

[engine-select] Preview engine selection <process>
- Select the configured preview engine before opening the new source @ viewer.PViewerEngineSelect(...)
> viewer-load-ownership

[viewer-load-ownership] Viewer request ownership <process>
- Advance the viewer load serial, stop its clock, clear inactive resume, and pause the current player @ viewer.PPlayerVideoLoad(...)
- Stop before starting the backend request if the viewer became unloaded, inactive, or superseded during preparation @ viewer.PPlayerVideoLoad(...)
> viewer-path-expectation

[viewer-path-expectation] Expected completion path <storage>
- Store a normalized expected source path for completion filtering, falling back to the original text when that normalization is rejected @ viewer.PPlayerVideoLoad(...)
> backend-start

[backend-start] Backend load dispatch <process>
- Start the asynchronous backend media-load operation for the requested source @ viewer.PPlayerVideoLoad(...)
> backend-path

[backend-path] Backend path normalization <decision>
- Normalize the requested source to a full path before establishing the load request @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
- Reject an invalid path immediately and cancel any current backend request @ media-load.LMediaLoadReject(...)
? "Path normalized" > backend-request
? "Invalid path syntax" > backend-failure-join [left]

[backend-request] Backend request ownership <process>
- Cancel and dispose the previous request, create a linked cancellation source, advance the generation, and mark the new request pending @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
> backend-source-check

[backend-source-check] Backend source validation <decision>
- Require a nonblank path, an existing file, and a supported media extension @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media.LMediaCheck(...)
? "Supported existing media" > ffprobe-read
? "Missing, blank, or unsupported" > backend-failure-join [left]

[ffprobe-read] FFprobe media inspection <external>
- Run the configured media reader off the caller thread with the request cancellation token @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
- Launch ffprobe for stream and format JSON on the source file @ media.LMediaFfprobeRead(...)
- Attach the ffprobe process to process custody @ custody.LCustodyAttach(...)
- Kill the entire ffprobe process tree when the request is cancelled @ media.LMediaFfprobeRead(...)
> ffprobe-result

[ffprobe-result] FFprobe result interpretation <process>
- Reject a nonzero ffprobe exit, empty output, or invalid JSON as a media-read failure @ media.LMediaFfprobeRead(...)
- Parse duration and the first video and audio stream information into LMediaInfo @ media.LMediaFfprobeParse(...)
> backend-current-check

[backend-current-check] Backend generation check <decision>
- Suppress a result when the loader was disposed or a newer generation superseded this request @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
  @ media-load.LMediaLoadFailCurrent(...)
- Classify cancellation for the current generation and preserve a successful parsed result only for the current request @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
? "Superseded or disposed" > obsolete-load
? "Current load failed or cancelled" > backend-failure-join [left]
? "Current media information" > backend-success

[backend-failure-join] Backend failures converge <junction>
> backend-failure

[backend-success] Backend media commit <storage>
- Clear pending state, store the current media path and media information, and create a successful load outcome @ media-load.LMediaLoadAsync(...)
> backend-success-ready

[obsolete-load] Obsolete backend result <output>
= A superseded or disposed backend request returns Obsolete without raising LMediaLoadCompleted.

[backend-failure] Backend failure publication <error>
- Clear pending state and create the current failure or cancellation outcome @ media-load.LMediaLoadFailCurrent(...)
- Raise an immediate path-normalization failure when normalization was rejected before a generation was established @ media-load.LMediaLoadReject(...)
> backend-completed-join

[backend-success-ready] Successful backend outcome ready <junction>
> backend-completed-join

[backend-completed-join] Backend outcomes converge <junction>
> backend-completed

[backend-completed] Backend completion event <process>
- Invoke each LMediaLoadCompleted subscriber independently and isolate subscriber exceptions @ media-load.LMediaLoadRaise(...)
> completion-filter

[completion-filter] Viewer completion acceptance <decision>
- Marshal backend completion onto the viewer dispatcher and compare viewer lifetime, load serial, and expected source path @ viewer.PViewerLoadHandle(...)
? "Viewer request is stale" > stale-result-join [left]
? "Current backend failure" > failed-status
? "Current backend success" > preview-engine

[failed-status] Unreadable media status <process>
- Publish a viewer cargo containing the failed source and backend error without media information or preview availability @ viewer.PViewerLoadHandle(...)
> media-status-join [right]

[preview-engine] Preview engine routing <decision>
- Route a successful media description to mpv when mpv is active, otherwise continue through Flyleaf @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
? "mpv active" > mpv-media-check
? "Flyleaf active" > flyleaf-media-join [right]

[mpv-media-check] mpv media eligibility <decision>
- Reject audio-only media when the current viewer does not permit audio-only sources @ viewer.PViewerMpvApply(...)
? "Audio-only source disallowed" > mpv-restricted-commit
? "Media allowed" > mpv-open

[mpv-open] mpv preview opening <external>
- Ensure an mpv player is attached to the current host, apply volume, and open the source on a worker task @ viewer.PViewerMpvApply(...)
> mpv-open-result

[mpv-restricted-commit] mpv restricted-source commit <process>
- Commit the source with no media information or preview and record the audio-only restriction @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
- Record the rejected media status in the log @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
> media-status-join [right]

[mpv-open-result] mpv opening result <decision>
- Discard the preview result if the viewer load serial or lifetime changed while mpv was opening @ viewer.PViewerMpvApply(...)
- Fall back to Flyleaf when mpv reports an opening error @ viewer.PViewerMpvApply(...)
? "Viewer request became stale" > stale-result-join [left]
? "mpv open failed" > mpv-fallback
? "mpv preview ready" > mpv-commit

[mpv-fallback] Flyleaf fallback from mpv <process>
- Dispose the mpv host and build a Flyleaf host for the same source @ viewer.PViewerMpvFallback(...)
> fallback-current-check

[mpv-commit] mpv viewer commit <process>
- Record the opened or rejected mpv media status in the log @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
- Commit media identity, preview visibility, stopped playback state, and nonpersistent crop reset @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
- Apply the preview state and either autoplay with the clock running or remain paused @ viewer.PViewerMpvCommit(...)
> media-status-join [right]

[fallback-current-check] Fallback request check <decision>
- Recheck the load serial and viewer lifetime before retrying the source through Flyleaf @ viewer.PViewerMpvFallback(...)
? "Viewer request still current" > flyleaf-media-join
? "Viewer request became stale" > stale-result-join [left]

[flyleaf-media-join] Flyleaf preview paths converge <junction>
> flyleaf-media-check

[flyleaf-media-check] Flyleaf media eligibility <decision>
- Reject audio-only media when the current viewer does not permit audio-only sources @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
? "Audio-only source disallowed" > flyleaf-restricted-commit
? "Media allowed" > flyleaf-open

[flyleaf-open] Flyleaf preview opening <external>
- Create or reuse a Flyleaf player, configure it, apply volume, and open the source @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
  @ viewer.PPlayerFlyleafOpen(...)
- Pause the opened player and seek to the start while recording any preview-opening error @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
  @ viewer.PPlayerStartPause(...)
> flyleaf-open-result

[flyleaf-restricted-commit] Flyleaf restricted-source commit <process>
- Record the rejected media status in the log @ viewer.PViewerMediaRecord(...)
- Commit the source with no media information or preview and record the audio-only restriction @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
> media-status-join [right]

[flyleaf-open-result] Flyleaf opening result <decision>
- Dispose a newly created unattached player when the viewer request became stale during preview opening @ viewer.PPlayerMediaApply(...)
? "Viewer request became stale" > stale-result-join [left]
? "Viewer request still current" > flyleaf-commit

[flyleaf-commit] Flyleaf viewer commit <process>
- Record the parsed media and preview availability in the log @ viewer.PViewerMediaRecord(...)
- Reuse or swap the Flyleaf player, synchronize the host, media identity, stopped playback state, and nonpersistent crop reset @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
- Restore preview state and either autoplay with the clock running or remain stopped when a preview player exists @ viewer.PViewerMediaCommit(...)
> media-status-join [right]

[stale-result-join] Stale preview outcomes converge <junction>
> stale-result

[media-status-join] Viewer commit outcomes converge <junction>
> media-status

[stale-result] Stale viewer result ignored <output>
= A completion or preview result belonging to an older or inactive viewer request does not replace the current viewer state.
[media-status] Viewer media publication <decision>
- Publish the resulting LCargo to every PViewerMediaChange subscriber @ viewer.PViewerMediaRaise(...)
? "Media information available" > loaded-fanout
? "Media information unavailable" > unavailable-fanout

[loaded-fanout] Loaded media synchronization <process>
= Subscribers independently synchronize their own state from the successful LCargo.
> loaded-viewer
> timeline-attached
> source-info-loaded
> workspace-loaded
> edit-restored

[unavailable-fanout] Unavailable media synchronization <process>
= Subscribers independently synchronize their own state from the LCargo without media information.
> unavailable-viewer
> timeline-cleared
> source-info-unavailable
> workspace-cleared
> edit-reset

[loaded-viewer] Viewer source available <output>
= The viewer identifies the loaded media and records whether a preview engine is available; autoplay determines whether playback begins immediately.

[timeline-attached] Active flow attached <output>
- Attach the media information and source path to the active flow at zero when the active window receives the media event @ window.PWindowMediaHandle(...)
= The active timeline is initialized for the loaded source.

[source-info-loaded] Source and Info synchronized <output>
- Show the loaded source path in an attached Source field @ source.PSourceMediaHandle(...)
- Show processability, preview availability, and parsed technical media information in an attached Info panel @ info.PInfoMediaHandle(...)
= Where those panels exist, they represent the loaded file.

[workspace-loaded] Workspace follow-up scheduled <output>
- Remember the newly loaded non-audio source and schedule LosslessCut-section discovery when its path changes @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaHandle(...)
- Restore relay sections after a relayed source successfully supplies media information @ workspace.PWorkspaceRelayApply(...)
= Workspace-specific post-load work is initiated only when applicable.

[edit-restored] Edit state restored <output>
- Restore the Edit tab's source-specific crop and edit plan after the media event @ edit.PEditCropRestore(...)
= Edit state follows the newly loaded source when the active surface is Edit.

[unavailable-viewer] Viewer media unavailable <output>
= A backend failure publishes the failed path without committing a new viewer source or media description; an audio-only restriction commits the source without usable media information or preview.

[timeline-cleared] Active flow cleared <output>
- Clear the active flow when the active window receives media status without media information @ window.PWindowMediaHandle(...)
= The active timeline has no loaded media description.

[source-info-unavailable] Source and Info report failure <output>
- Synchronize an attached Source field with the reported source path @ source.PSourceMediaHandle(...)
- Show the backend or preview restriction error and unavailable status in an attached Info panel @ info.PInfoMediaHandle(...)
= Where those panels exist, the visible source status reports that media information is unavailable.

[workspace-cleared] Workspace media follow-up cleared <output>
- Clear the remembered LosslessCut source when media information or a source path is unavailable @ workspace.PWorkspaceMediaHandle(...)
= No LosslessCut discovery is scheduled for the failed status.

[edit-reset] Edit state re-evaluated <output>
- Re-evaluate Edit crop restoration after the failed or restricted media event @ edit.PEditCropRestore(...)
= On Edit, restoration runs against the viewer state that remains after that event.

